// @vibe/compiler/checker — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal contract.
// Directory-shared-scope package: the core expression/statement checker
// (checker.vibe, checker_stmt.vibe) and type-expr resolution
// (checker_resolve.vibe). The builtin signature tables live in
// @vibe/compiler/checker/builtin_sigs, pattern checking and exhaustiveness in
// @vibe/compiler/checker/patterns, trait bounds and the Send judgment in
// @vibe/compiler/checker/traits, and
// the effect/mutability passes in @vibe/compiler/checker/effects;
// checker_effects.vibe re-exports the part of the latter declared below. checker_facade.vibe (see naming note below)
// re-exports a SUBSET of the surface (check_expr,
// check_pattern, pat_has_unsupported_or_binding, resolve_type_expr,
// CheckedProgram, check_program, check_program_result,
// check_program_type_table, check_program_with_env,
// check_program_with_env_result, check_stmts,
// canonical_retained_trait_impl_entries_snapshot, canonical_retained_trait_method_gens_snapshot, canonical_checked_type_defs_snapshot, canonical_checked_value_env_snapshot, canonical_effective_value_env_snapshot, and the narrowly scoped type-definition observation APIs) via the `export ./file.vibe { names }`
// SReExport form (#726);
// every other name below is defined directly (`export fn`) in its own
// sibling file and reaches outside importers purely through this package's
// directory-shared scope + the facade generated from THIS contract (not
// from checker_facade.vibe's own hand-written re-export list, which the
// generated facade supersedes at ingestion time) — same shape as
// codegen/expr's expr.vibe/core.vibe/support.vibe split.
//
// Naming-collision note: the established rename convention for this
// migration batch is `git mv index.vibe <dirname>.vibe` (see
// codegen/expr/expr.vibe, codegen/gc/gc.vibe, syntax/syntax.vibe). For this
// directory the dirname is "checker", but `checker/checker.vibe` already
// exists as a substantial (5.3k line) real implementation file — the core
// expression checker, not a facade — so `git mv index.vibe checker.vibe`
// would silently clobber it. `validate_index_layout_fs` also forbids
// index.vibe and index.vpkg coexisting in the same directory ("a boundary
// has exactly one index"), so leaving index.vibe in place unrenamed was not
// an option either (loader/index.vibe::desugar_contract_source_fs). The old
// index.vibe was therefore renamed to `checker_facade.vibe` instead —
// non-colliding, and its content did not need any other change: directory
// auto-discovery (`contract_sibling_impl_raws`) already reaches every other
// sibling file regardless of what checker_facade.vibe itself re-exports, so
// the facade file's existing partial re-export list stays correct as-is.
//
// Compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `checker`): the old single `checker/index.vibe` row becomes a
// dual row (this contract + checker_facade.vibe); every other impl file in
// this directory has its own manifest row.

